  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mobility plan for bicycle use along the BRT in Dakar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Senegalese Urban Transport Authority (CETUD) requested the advice of Dutch experts to develop a mobility plan to increase the safe use of bicycles in Dakar. This project helps CETUD to promote the use of (shared) bicycles as an alternative mode of transportation to the automobile in safe and pleasant conditions and contributes to the improvement of inter-modality along the Bus Rapid Transit (BRT) corridor in Dakar, Senegal. The mobility plan includes an inventory to implement a shared bicycle system and a communication plan to raise awareness among the population. The eventual implementation of the plan should reduce traffic in Dakar, reduce emissions, improve accessibility, and create jobs like bicycle sales, and rent and repair shops.</narrative>
  </description>
